---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | ShipToCash"
  description="Peng Zhou writes ShipToCash — practical guides that take vibe coders from localhost to a live, earning app."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-10">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-ink-900 mb-8">About ShipToCash</h1>

    <div class="prose">
      <div class="flex items-start gap-6 not-prose mb-8">
        <img
          src={SITE.avatar}
          alt={`${SITE.author}, founder of ShipToCash`}
          width="112"
          height="112"
          loading="lazy"
          class="rounded-full shadow-md flex-shrink-0"
          style="width: 112px; height: 112px;"
        />
        <div class="flex-1">
          <p class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink-900 mb-1">{SITE.author}</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-500 mb-3">Vibe coder &middot; Founder of ShipToCash</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p>
        Hi, I'm Peng Zhou. I build small software products, and I write about the
        unglamorous part nobody teaches you: getting an app actually <em>deployed</em>,
        taking real money from real users, and not getting into legal trouble doing it.
      </p>
      <p>
        ShipToCash focuses on deployment, checkout integration, and the operational steps
        between a working prototype and a public product. This site itself uses Astro
        to generate static pages, with its content maintained in a Git repository.
      </p>
      <h2 id="editorial-standards">Editorial standards</h2>
      <p>
        Guides combine explanations, documentation references, and worked examples.
        An example is not a report of a customer transaction or a production test.
        Where a guide describes a recorded test, it should identify the environment,
        steps, and observed result. We do not claim every service or scenario has been
        tested on the author's own account.
      </p>
      <p>
        AI tools assist with drafting and code review. AI output is not evidence of
        first-hand experience. Prices, limits, eligibility, and API behavior should be
        checked against the linked provider documentation and your own account before use.
        Publication dates describe publication; update dates describe edits, not necessarily
        a complete retest of every step.
      </p>
      <p>
        Hypothetical calculations are labelled as examples. Payment and business-structure
        articles distinguish provider responsibilities from the seller's local obligations.
        ShipToCash does not provide individualized legal or tax advice.
      </p>
      <p>
        When a material error is reported, we review the relevant instructions and update
        the page. Please use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> to identify the URL,
        affected step, and supporting documentation. If an article contains a paid or affiliate
        relationship, it should disclose that relationship beside the relevant recommendation.
      </p>
      <p>
        I also write about AI tools over at
        <a
          href="https://aikitguides.com"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-700 underline">AI Kit Guides</a>
        — same person, different lane. If you're still picking the tools themselves, that's a
        good place to start.
      </p>

      <h2>Recorded verification lab</h2>
      <p>
        The payment and delivery guides include a
        <a href="https://github.com/zhoupeng20188/shiptocash-verification-labs/tree/6537765e7d9493673e744602e388f5cd06b7a2c9/payment-delivery-lab">separate source repository</a>
        with fixed versions, commands, source hashes, and a recorded 45-check run.
        These are synthetic local experiments, not real customer transactions.
        Start with the <a href="/payments/lemon-squeezy-webhook-signature-astro/">webhook case</a>
        or the <a href="/payments/send-download-link-after-payment-no-backend/">download case</a>
        to see what was measured and what remains outside the experiment.
      </p>

      <h2>What you'll find here</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Deploy</strong> — hosting, domains, HTTPS, databases</li>
        <li><strong>Payments</strong> — Stripe, Paddle, Lemon Squeezy, taxes (and what to do when Stripe says no)</li>
        <li><strong>Monetize</strong> — ads, subscriptions, pricing</li>
        <li><strong>Tools</strong> — fee calculations with editable assumptions</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        Found a broken step? Built something with one of these guides? I'd love to hear about it.
        The fastest way to reach me is on
        <a
          href={SITE.github}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-700 underline">GitHub</a>,
        or through the <a href="/contact/" class="text-brand-600 hover:text-brand-700 underline">contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
